# Line endings. Every commit in this repo has warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF"
# because the policy was implicit; this makes it explicit before the first push,
# when it costs nothing.
#
# Text is stored LF in the repo and checked out CRLF on Windows, which is the git
# default for a Windows-only project. Existing blobs are left alone — run
# `git add --renormalize .` if you ever want the history's line endings unified too.
* text=auto

# PowerShell must be CRLF on disk. Some Windows PowerShell hosts mis-parse a
# script with bare LF endings, and dev\revit.ps1 is the script that drives Revit.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary, never diffed or line-ending mangled.
*.png binary
*.rvt binary
*.bundle binary

# Git hooks are run by sh and break on CRLF, so they are LF on disk regardless of platform.
ci/hooks/* text eol=lf
